      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im having an issue with our sublimation heat press setup in our facility. the colors arent transferring deep enough into the polyester fabric, it looks really faded and washed out even when we run it through twice. what should i be checking for regarding temp and pressure settings?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To begin troubleshooting, verify that the sublimation temperature is set accurately according to the polyester fabric’s dimensions for optimal transfer. Typically, sublimation temperatures range from 288° F to 324° F (with a contact temperature of 250-300° F). Make sure your pressure setting is also at the appropriate level, generally 15-25 PSI, depending on the fabric thickness. This should ensure a deeper color transfer and a sharper finish on your polyester sublimation garments.",
